## Why This Is Asked
OTCA cross-tenant logging scenario focusing on verifiable data erasure and auditable provenance, not just privacy.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA residency enforcement and tenant scoping
- Deletion workflows, deletion certificates, and verifiable erasure
- Edge DP masking of sensitive fields before transport
- Immutable audit ledger with cryptographic proofs
- Per-tenant retention policies and tombstoning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: handleDeletion(tenantId, rideId)
function handleDeletion(tenantId, rideId){
  regionStore.erase(tenantId, rideId);
  const cert = createDeletionCert(tenantId, rideId, hash(regionStore.snapshot()));
  auditLog.append(cert);
  centralLedger.commit(cert);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test audit-log immutability under clock skew and partial failures?
- How would you handle cross-region deletion consistency during network partitions?
